Local fault cases additionally cover:
  Canceled finish HTTP context still leaves retryable durable intent.
  Finish transient failure and Gateway controller reopen.
  Finish persistence failure before write / after write / after fsync:
  complete surviving frames revalidated/fsynced and operation released.

Issues found and corrected during this run:
  Old version-rejection test assumed pending version 2 was always invalid;
  version 2 is now restricted control-only data, unknown version test uses 3.
  Idle finishing worker contended with new requests; changed to wake only
  for requested/persisted finishing and back off only while work remains.
  Cold terminal/local unfinished restart originally had no reconciliation;
  now exact receipt plus proved checkpoint restores the local terminal frame.
  New recovery test setup needed valid segment budget and pre-existing binding;
  fixed fixture setup, without weakening production binding checks.
  Delayed EVAL test initially expected marker no-op despite changed value;
  actual script checks value first. Assert changed-value rejection and also
  assert same-value existing-marker no-op; neither emits another marker SET.

